---
import '../styles/prose.css';

import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { unlistedApps } from '../data/policies';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const appName = unlistedApps['convertit-ios'].name;
const privacyPath = '/convertit-ios-privacy/';

const lastUpdated = new Date('2026-11-21T08:50:00Z');
const lastUpdatedDisplay = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
  hour: '2-digit',
  minute: '2-digit',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
  timeZoneName: 'short',
}).format(lastUpdated);

const title = `${appName} terms of service`;
const description =
  'Terms of service for Convertit for iPhone and iPad by The Byte Array Ltd: App Store purchases, the 24-hour pass, your licence, your files stay on your device, refunds through Apple, and your statutory rights.';
---

<!-- This URL is for the App Store listing and the in-app paywall; keep the path stable. -->
<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Legal', path: '/legal/' },
    { name: title, path: Astro.url.pathname },
  ]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl pt-4 sm:pt-10" data-pagefind-body>
    <Breadcrumbs
      items={[{ label: 'Legal', href: '/legal/' }, { label: title }]}
    />

    <header class="mt-6 sm:mt-8">
      <h1
        class="font-display text-page-title text-balance"
      >
        {title}
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-label-lg text-on-surface-variant">
        Last updated <time datetime={lastUpdated.toISOString()}>{lastUpdatedDisplay}</time>
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose mt-10 sm:mt-12">
      <section>
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Convertit for iPhone and iPad (“the App”) is published by {site.company.name}, a company registered
          in {site.company.jurisdiction} (company number{' '}
          <a href={site.company.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link">{site.company.number}</a>),
          with its registered office at {site.company.office}. In these terms, “we” and “us” mean{' '}
          {site.company.name}, and “you” means the person using the App.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>These terms</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are the licence agreement for the App. By downloading, buying or using it, you agree to
          them. If you do not agree, do not use the App. They sit alongside our{' '}
          <a href={privacyPath} class="text-link">privacy policy</a>, which is part of your agreement with us.
          Our <a href="/terms/" class="text-link">site terms</a> cover this website. Where the two differ, these
          terms apply to the App.
        </p>
        <p>
          These terms are between you and us only, not with Apple. We, not Apple, are solely responsible for
          the App and its content. Your use of the App must also follow the Usage Rules in the{' '}
          <a
            href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="text-link"
          >Apple Media Services Terms and Conditions</a>, including Family Sharing where it applies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What the App does</h2>
        <p>
          The App is an offline audio and video toolkit for iPhone and iPad. It converts audio and video,
          compresses video, makes GIFs, edits tags and includes related tools, and everything runs on your
          device. Many tools are free. The Pro tools are marked with a lock in the App.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Pro and the 24-hour pass</h2>
        <p>The Pro tools are unlocked by one of two in-app purchases, both sold by Apple through the App Store:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Pro forever:</strong> a one-time purchase that unlocks the Pro tools on the App for as long
            as you use it, including future updates.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>24-hour pass:</strong> unlocks the Pro tools for 24 hours from the moment of purchase. It
            does not renew and you are never charged again. You can buy another pass later or buy Pro forever
            at any time.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Prices are shown in the App and on the App Store in your currency before you pay. Apple handles the
          payment and any tax, and we never see your payment details. There are no subscriptions and no other
          charges.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pro forever is linked to your Apple Account. If you reinstall the App or use another iPhone or iPad
          with the same Apple Account, use Restore purchase in the App. A pass that has already ended cannot be
          restored.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your purchase unlocks the Pro tools as they are in the App as of 21 November 2026. We may add new
          tools later. Any that are sold separately will be marked in the App before any charge, so a future
          tool is never billed without notice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Refunds</h2>
        <p>
          Because Apple handles payment, refunds are requested from Apple at{' '}
          <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link"
            >reportaproblem.apple.com</a
          >, under Apple’s rules. We cannot issue App Store refunds ourselves. If something in the App does not
          work, please contact us as well, so we can fix it. Nothing here removes any refund right you have by
          law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your licence</h2>
        <p>
          We give you a personal, non-transferable, non-exclusive licence to use the App on Apple devices that
          you own or control, as permitted by the Usage Rules in the Apple Media Services Terms and
          Conditions. You may not sell, rent, lend, sub-license or redistribute the App, or copy it except as
          normal use and the law allow.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may not reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the App, except where applicable law
          expressly permits it (for example, to achieve interoperability). The App includes open-source
          components that are licensed to you under their own licences, which are listed in the App under
          About › Open-source licenses. Nothing in these terms limits or overrides your rights under those
          licences.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your files</h2>
        <p>
          You keep ownership of the files you open and the files the App produces. The App processes your
          files on your device and does not upload them to us or to anyone else. You are responsible for
          keeping your own backups and for having the right to use the files you process. See our{' '}
          <a href={privacyPath} class="text-link">privacy policy</a> for how the App handles data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Updates and support</h2>
        <p>
          We, not Apple, are responsible for maintaining and supporting the App. Apple has no obligation to
          provide any maintenance or support for it. Contact us from the App (About › Contact support) or by
          email with the steps to reproduce the problem. We aim to reply within 5 business days and to fix it or
          provide a workaround within 14 business days.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Warranties and your statutory rights</h2>
        <p>
          We provide the App with reasonable care and skill, but we cannot promise it is error-free or that it
          will work on every device or with every file. As far as the law allows, the App is provided “as is”
          and we exclude other warranties and conditions that would otherwise apply.
        </p>
        <p>
          If the App fails to conform to any warranty that applies, you may notify Apple, and Apple will refund
          the purchase price you paid for it. To the maximum extent permitted by law, Apple has no other
          warranty obligation for the App, and any other claims, losses, liabilities, damages, costs or
          expenses caused by a failure to conform to a warranty are our responsibility, not Apple’s.
        </p>
        <p>
          None of this affects your statutory rights. If you are a consumer, the Consumer Rights Act 2015
          requires digital content to be as described, fit for purpose and of satisfactory quality, and nothing
          in these terms removes or limits those rights.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Our liability</h2>
        <p>
          We do not exclude or limit our liability where it would be unlawful to do so. This includes liability
          for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, and, if you are a consumer, for
          damage to your device or to other digital content caused by our failure to use reasonable care and
          skill.
        </p>
        <p>
          Subject to that, we are not liable for loss that was not reasonably foreseeable, for loss of data you
          could have backed up, or for indirect or consequential loss. Our total liability in connection with
          the App is limited to the amount you paid for it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Claims about the App</h2>
        <p>
          We, not Apple, are responsible for addressing any claims by you or a third party relating to the App or
          your possession or use of it. This includes product liability claims, any claim that the App fails to
          conform to an applicable legal or regulatory requirement, and claims under consumer protection,
          privacy or similar laws.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a third party claims that the App or your possession or use of it infringes their intellectual
          property rights, we, not Apple, are solely responsible for investigating, defending, settling and
          discharging that claim.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Legal compliance</h2>
        <p>
          You confirm that you are not located in a country that is subject to a United States Government
          embargo or that has been designated by the United States Government as a “terrorist supporting”
          country, and that you are not listed on any United States Government list of prohibited or restricted
          parties.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Termination</h2>
        <p>
          You can stop using the App at any time by deleting it. We may end your licence only if you materially
          breach these terms; we will not arbitrarily withdraw a licence you have paid for. If your licence
          ends, you must stop using the App. Any refund right you have already earned, and your statutory
          rights, are not affected.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We version this page. See the Last updated date and time above. If we make a material change, we add a
          dated note here and announce it on our blog at least 7 days before it takes effect. A change will not
          reduce what Pro forever covers. Continuing to use the App after a change takes effect means you accept
          the updated terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Apple as a third-party beneficiary</h2>
        <p>
          Apple and Apple’s subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these terms. Once you accept them,
          Apple has the right, and is deemed to have accepted the right, to enforce these terms against you as a
          third-party beneficiary.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and disputes are subject to the courts of
          England and Wales. If you are a consumer living in Scotland or Northern Ireland, you can also bring
          proceedings in your local courts, and you keep the benefit of any mandatory consumer protections that
          apply where you live.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions, complaints or claims about the App go to {site.company.name}, {site.company.office}. You can
          also use our <a href="/contact/" class="text-link">contact form</a> or email us at{' '}
          <button type="button" data-mailto={site.mail} class="text-link">{site.emailDisplay}</button>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
